Ladybird keeps a content-sized absolutely positioned block indefinite
while laying out its children, so cyclic percentage heights behave as
auto. Heights resolved before that layout remain definite, including
stretch-fit heights and heights derived from a preferred aspect ratio.

Blink separates these paths in CanComputeBlockSizeWithoutLayout() and
ComputeOofBlockDimensions(): A fit-content automatic height requires
layout without a fixed block size. Gecko makes the same distinction in
nsIFrame::ComputeAbsolutePosAutoSize(), leaving content-sized heights
unconstrained while resolving stretch and aspect-ratio sizes up front.

WebKit recomputes an out-of-flow height in RenderBlock::
availableLogicalHeightForPercentageComputation() when RenderBox::
hasFullyConstrainedLogicalHeight() finds two specified block insets.
That predicate has no alignment check. Ladybird follows the cyclic-
percentage rule and the Chrome measurements for this case: A percentage-
height child with 60px of content stays 60px inside an anchor-centered
content-sized parent, including when the parent has a 120px minimum.
